[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720065501","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2720065501","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2720065501,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iIOfd","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T05:57:55Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T05:57:55Z","body":"For consistency, should we capitalize the `namespace godot` in godot-cpp as well?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720065501/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721641337","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2721641337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2721641337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iOPN5","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T15:20:17Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T15:20:17Z","body":"> For consistency, should we capitalize the `namespace godot` in godot-cpp as well?\r\n\r\nI don't think we should do this at this point.\r\n\r\nIf Godot does end up making a `Godot` namespace where everything lives (which I'd personally like :-)), then, yes, we should change godot-cpp to be consistent.\r\n\r\nHowever, at this point, we'll only have `Godot::String` from PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104040, which is actually just an alias, the `String` class is still declared at the global scope, and the \"official\" API is to use it at the global scope and not using `Godot::String`.\r\n\r\nSo, at this point, changing godot-cpp to use `Godot` rather than `godot` doesn't make its API any more consistent with Godot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721641337/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721704616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2721704616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2721704616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iOeqo","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T15:41:17Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T15:41:17Z","body":"> However, at this point, we'll only have `Godot::String` from PR #104040, which is actually just an alias, the `String` class is still declared at the global scope, and the \"official\" API is to use it at the global scope and not using `Godot::String`.\r\n\r\nIt's not sure that it would get merged, as this screams as a \"hack\".","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721704616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722075160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2722075160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2722075160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iP5IY","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T17:20:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T17:20:11Z","body":"Worth mentioning that snake_case seems to be the dominant naming convention for namespaces in C++ as far as I can tell, both in third-party libraries and the built-in `std::` namespace. Also, a similarly-cased language, Rust, uses snake_case for namespaces, since in that language they correspond with file names. So I suppose this PR is going against the grain.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722075160/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722236044","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2722236044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2722236044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iQgaM","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T17:52:32Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T17:52:32Z","body":"> So I suppose this PR is going against the grain.\r\n\r\nGoing against the grain just makes our namespaces more unique ;-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722236044/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":4,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724877211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104043#issuecomment-2724877211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104043","id":2724877211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ialOb","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-14T14:27:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-14T14:27:20Z","body":"There's also the prospect of us standardizing under snake_case instead! It was only discussed that we don't have a standard implementation, not necessarily what that implementation should be. Opting for snake_case changes more files iirc, but a good chunk of those are the test headers which would be entirely removed when eventually converted to source files.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2724877211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]